      "message": "lgtm. I suspect that the actual operation/stage will be slightly more complex. In the old stack interpreter, the corresponding instruction(s) [1] handled several things at once (because they\u0027re always clumped together in code-gen):\n\n- Store the current mask value to the mask stack\n- Take the most recently evaluated condition (old code got this from the value stack, new code probably gets it from \u0027r\u0027) ... turn it into a mask, stored at the new top of the stack (which would mean moving it to \u0027dr\u0027 here)\n\n[1] https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/356921/5/src/sksl/SkSLByteCode.cpp#b833",
